###### 6. Corrosion Control 

For control of the corrosion, a selection may be made from among the following measures: 

1. Choice of a different material. Application of another more corrosion-resistant material. However, the choice of material is determined not only by the corrosion resistance but also by the mechanical properties and economic considerations. 

2. Design modifications. By adapting the design, treatment, and construction, the part of the system can be rendered less vulnerable to corrosion. 

